kevin: Quick note — found a small but consistent repro in the node sampleapp where an auth refresh that triggers an immediate reconnect can cause fragment reordering. Repro attached below.

anika: Can you paste the tiny repro and logs? Is this Node-only?

kevin: Node-only so far. Repro harness loops EventSource connects with short jitter and forces token rotation mid-stream. Script: 
```
// fast-drain-poc.js
const {EventSource} = require('eventsource');
async function loop(url){
  for(let i=0;i<500;i++){
    const es = new EventSource(url);
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100));
    es.close();
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 80 + Math.random()*80));
  }
}
loop(process.env.URL);
```
Logs (trimmed): partial fragment F1 arrives, auth refresh fires, client starts new conn and parser instance, fragment F2 from new conn parsed, then leftover F1-tail arrives from old socket -> parser emits F2 then F1-tail -> leads to duplicate close token or garbled JSON.

oscar: Hmm, sounds like the old socket isn't drained before the new parser begins consuming. Did you try the SDK's buffering and parity flags?

kevin: Yes. Turning on `bufferChunks` reduces freq but doesn't fix it. The crux is parser swap happens before ensuring the previous socket's 'end' has been processed.

anika: Short-term mitigation ideas: 1) server-side: emit an explicit flush event before auth rotation to provide a clean delimiter; 2) client-side: add a small drain-window (e.g., 50ms) where new parser waits for any stray data from old socket, configurable via flag `drainWindowMs`.

oscar: Another cheap client-side fix: server include monotonic `x-frag-id` per chunk; client drops fragments with id <= lastSeen when reconnect detected. That avoids duplicate final emits while we fix parser reassembly.

kevin: I prototyped `drainWindowMs` in the sampleapp and a `dropStaleFragmentIds` toggle. In my loop, enabling both reduced incidents to zero. Drain window adds a tiny tail latency (median +6ms) in worst case.

anika: Good. Can you open a PR with both behind feature flags default-off and add an e2e job that randomizes auth rotation timing? We'll want this in CI to track regressions.

patch-bot: Created RED-7122 "node sampleapp: fast reconnect -> SSE fragment reorder" and attached logs + repro script.

oscar: For long term: parser should be able to reassemble fragments across reconnects when a resume token/Last-Event-Id is present, but that requires server-side cooperation to provide per-fragment ids and resume metadata. Also audit auth refresh path: calling `abort()` currently may leave buffered bytes unprocessed; consider signaling `finishSegment` before aborting.

kevin: I'll open the PR today with: (a) `drainWindowMs` default 0, env var SAMPLEAPP_DRAIN_MS; (b) server header `x-frag-id` support + client drop-stale option; (c) e2e job devex/reconnect-drain-window in sampleapp CI. Assigning reviewers @anika and @oscar.

anika: Please include a manual test note and link RED-7122 in PR description. Also add a short unit test that simulates tail arrival after parser swap.

oscar: I'll add a lib-level test for fragment-id ordering once the PR lands.

qa-bot: Adding nightly flaky job devex/reconnect-drain-randomized that fails on duplicate final tokens.

kevin: Thanks 8077; ping when CI green and I'll drop the repro in devex/sampleapp/repro/fast-drain-poc.js.
